==English==
[[File:Geranium wilfordii (sepal).JPG|thumb|<center>The ''perianth'' of this flower includes the pale [[petal]]s and the green [[sepal]]s. The rest of the flower on the far side of the petals is not part of the '''perianth'''.</center>]]
[[File:Blepharostoma trichophyllum (d, 144542-474731) 9814.JPG|thumb|<center>A mature spore of the [[liverwort]] ''[[Blepharostoma]] trichophyllum'' in its '''perianth'''</center>]]
===Etymology===
From {{confix|en|peri|anth}}, thus "around the flower.", from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|périanthe}}, from {{etyl|NL.|en}} {{m|la|perianthium}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|botany}} The [[sterile]] parts of a [[flower]]; collectively, the [[sepal]]s and [[petal]]s (or [[tepal]]s).
# {{lb|en|botany|bryology}} The sterile, tubelike [[tissue]] that surrounds the female reproductive structure in a leafy [[liverwort]].
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae|volume=V|page=5|text=Archegonia are surrounded early in their development by the juvenile '''perianth''', through the slender beak of which the elongated neck of the fertilized archegonium protrudes.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|perigone}}

